<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The small coloured dot in the status chip over the live map ("● LIVE GPS", "● LOCATING…",
    "● NO GPS FIX").

    Deliberately colourless here: the fill is a placeholder that AddPlaceFragment tints from code,
    because on this chip the *colour is the status* — blue for a live or demo fix, the accent while a
    fix is being looked for, coral when there is none. Three static drawables would say the same
    thing three times and let one of them drift.

    No ring, unlike bg_gps_dot: at 7dp across, a 2.5dp ring would leave almost no colour to see.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="oval">

    <solid android:color="@color/here_dot" />

</shape>
